            "question": "What does the HVHZ change when I order a glass railing in Miami?",
            "answer": "<p>The heights do not change; the review does. Miami-Dade's building departments apply the High-Velocity Hurricane Zone rules of the Florida Building Code. That means stricter wind-load requirements and a close look at how the spigots attach. The department may ask for engineering with the permit. Our engineering documents cover top-mount and side-mount spigots on concrete and on wood. Ask the building department what it wants before you order.</p>",
