          "settings": {
            "question": "My Brickell balcony is a concrete slab. Which spigot do I use?",
            "answer": "<p>Both work on concrete. The 6-inch top-mount spigot bolts down into the slab. The side-mount spigot fixes to the slab edge and keeps the full balcony floor, which matters on a narrow balcony. The engineering documents give the blocking and anchor details for concrete; the fasteners themselves are sold separately. Check the slab edge thickness before choosing side-mount, and send photos if you are unsure.</p>",
            "pages": ""
