            "question": "Does Coral Gables review a glass railing differently from the City of Miami?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Coral Gables is its own city with its own building department and a Board of Architects that reviews exterior changes to homes. The City of Miami, Miami Beach and Key Biscayne each run their own permit counters, and unincorporated Miami-Dade goes through the county. All of them apply the same HVHZ code, but the forms and the review steps differ. Check with the office that covers your address first.</p>",
