        "t1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Brickell towers, Gables homes and rooftop terraces</strong></p><p>Miami is a city of balconies. Brickell and Edgewater towers line Biscayne Bay with concrete balconies on every floor. A frameless glass balcony railing opens the view when an association updates the facade. Across the causeways, Miami Beach condos face the Atlantic. Key Biscayne sits at the end of the Rickenbacker Causeway, with its own village building department. Coral Gables and Coconut Grove are house country: pool decks under banyan trees, raised terraces on the bay and open stairs in renovated Mediterranean homes.</p><p>Wynwood, Little River and Buena Vista have new townhomes with rooftop terraces, where a glass railing keeps the skyline view. Pinecrest and Palmetto Bay add big lots with pools. Everywhere, the air carries salt, the sun is strong year-round and summer brings daily rain. That is why every spigot and connector we sell is 2205 stainless and every panel is 12 mm tempered glass.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>The HVHZ and the Miami-Dade code</strong></p><p>Miami-Dade County is in the High-Velocity Hurricane Zone of the Florida Building Code, 8th edition (2023). The HVHZ has stricter wind-load rules than the rest of the state. The building department reviews how each spigot attaches and may ask for engineering documents. Our <a href=\"/pages/glass-railing-engineering-testing\">engineering documents</a> cover top-mount and side-mount spigots on concrete and on wood, with testing and blocking details. Miami, Miami Beach, Coral Gables and Key Biscayne each have their own building department; unincorporated addresses go through the county.</p><p>A house needs a 36-inch guard on a deck or balcony more than 30 inches above grade; condos and other multifamily buildings need 42 inches. Pool barriers follow the Residential Swimming Pool Safety Act: 48 inches on the outside, with gates that close on their own and open away from the pool. See our <a href=\"/pages/florida-building-code-for-glass-railings\">Florida building code page</a>, then confirm with the building department.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Delivery and installation in Miami</strong></p><p>Standard orders are processed in 2 to 3 business days. They reach Miami-Dade in 5 to 10 business days by freight carrier with a liftgate. At a house, the crate comes down to the driveway. At a Brickell or Edgewater tower, the driver needs the loading dock. Book it with building management and tell us the address type when you order. Custom sizes take 2 to 3 weeks in transit. Orders over 3,000 dollars ship free, and the checkout price is final: no duties, tariffs or hidden fees.</p><p>Installation is DIY with the installation guide and videos, and a standard railing takes about 4 hours. On a concrete balcony, top-mount spigots anchor into the slab; side-mount spigots fix to the slab edge when you want the floor clear. Fasteners are sold separately. Report damage within 3 days of delivery and before installation for a free replacement or refund.</p>"
          }
        }
